 s: Law\, Policy\nDetails: https://www.law.cam.ac.uk/events/law-and-climate
 -crisis-seminars-change-and-tort-law\nSign-up needed\nDate/time: \n\n Frid
 ay 5 February 2027 \n\n 4:00pm to 5:00pm\n\n Location: \n\n David Attenbor
 ough Building\n\n About \n\n Speaker: Lord Philip Sales (United Kingdom Su
 preme Court)\n The Cambridge Seminar Series on Law and the Climate Crisis 
 explores the vital role of legal systems in tackling one of the most press
 ing issues of our time.\n This series brings together top experts in law a
 nd climate action to discuss how climate change interacts with specific ar
 eas of law\, setting out both how legal fields are being impacted by clima
 te change and how the law can help drive climate action.\n The Cambridge S
 eminar Series on Law and the Climate Crisis is co-hosted by the Centre for
  Climate Engagement at Hughes Hall\, Cambridge Zero\, the Centre for Envir
 onment\, Energy and Natural Resource Governance (CEENRG)\, the Cambridge C
 limate Society\, the Lauterpacht Centre for International Law\, and the Ne
 t Zero Lawyers
